## 6. Topology Emergence: Role Sampling with Qualitative Logic

### 6.1 Role Sampling Prompt

Instead of a probability matrix, use an LLM call to decide the next node's role:

```text
You are a Propagation Topology Planner. Given the current state of a 
data visualization propagation chain, you decide what type of actor 
is most likely to pick up and modify this visualization next.

## Current Chain State
- Topic: {topic}
- Topic controversy level: {controversy_level}
- Current node role: {current_role}
- Current node platform: {current_platform}
- Chain depth so far: {depth}
- Roles already in chain: {role_sequence}

## Taxonomy Knowledge: Propagation Patterns (from 22-case corpus)

Role transition frequencies (empirical):

1. After a BRIDGER (82.0% of source roles):
   - → Amplifier: 34.4% (most common single transition)
   - → Bridger: 24.6% (legitimacy transfer, usually minor shifts)
   - → Extender: 19.7% (scope broadening)
   - → Adverser: 3.3% (very rare, only in highly polarized topics 
     like climate denial or pandemic misinformation)

2. After an AMPLIFIER (13.1% of source roles):
   - → Amplifier: 8.2% (cumulative drift, usually minor per step)
   - → Extender: 3.3% (broadening after amplification)
   - → Adverser: 1.6% (very uncommon, only 1 case observed)

3. After an EXTENDER (4.9% of source roles):
   - → Amplifier: 3.3% (emphasize the extended frame)
   - → Extender: 1.6% (rare double-extension)

4. After an ADVERSER: Propagation **TERMINATES** (100% terminal rate 
   in the corpus). Zero adverser nodes appear as source for subsequent 
   edges. If forced to continue, only an Amplifier forwarding the 
   adversarial frame with minor changes is plausible.

Topology patterns:
- Tree topology (81.8% of cases): single source fans out to 2-4 variants
- Linear topology (18.2%): sequential chain, typical depth 2-5
- Median variants per case: 3 (range: 1-5)
- Maximum observed depth: 5 (C08 immigration case)

Additional factors:
- Deeper chains (depth > 3) are more likely to involve Amplifiers 
  (cumulative drift pattern)
- Highly controversial topics are more likely to eventually attract 
  an Adverser (but still rare — only 3 of 22 cases have adverser nodes)
- Chains rarely exceed depth 5 in the corpus

Platform selection guidance:
- If current platform is T1, next is most likely T2 (news media) or T3
- News Media acts as intermediary: receives from T1, forwards to T3
- Social Media and Online Community are common endpoints (net sinks)
- Backward flow (T3→T1) is rare (3.3% of edges)

## Output Format
Respond in JSON:
{
  "next_role": "bridger|amplifier|extender|adverser",
  "should_terminate": true|false,
  "next_platform_type": "suggested platform type",
  "reasoning": "..."
}
```

